## Validation

- Local governance/security tests: 10 passed
- Production dependency audit: 0 vulnerabilities
- VS Code diagnostics: 0 errors
- Public `/api/health`: HTTP 200
- Mission Control shell: HTTP 200 with Morgan Trust Center
- Public static preview: HTTP 200 with static-data disclaimer
- Protected `/api/readiness`: HTTP 401 without authorization; live status `ready` with scheduled authorization
- Protected `/approvals`: HTTP 401 without authorization
- Protected App Service `/responses`: HTTP 401 without authorization
- Protected `/agentic-kanban`: HTTP 401 without authorization
- Teams call control: the EasyAuth-protected, finance-operator-only, same-origin Mission Control button now treats the explicit click as authorization for one immediate call; model and scheduler outbound calls remain L2-gated
- Live Teams readiness: ACS, federation resource marker, public callback host, and realtime voice configuration all report ready
- Teams 403/10391 remediation: the configured target had the resource-account `PHONESYSTEM_VIRTUALUSER` plan and was interpreted by Teams as `PureOnlineApplicationInstance`; it was atomically changed to the available human Teams Phone Standard (`MCOEV`) license, Enterprise Voice was reasserted, and Teams now reports `PureOnlineTeamsOnlyUser` with SIP and registrar provisioning
- Federation proof: the App Service connection string matches the allowlisted ACS resource, the authoritative immutable resource ID is present in the Teams global allowlist, and the target's global external-access policy enables ACS federation
- Local end-to-end gate test: request → signed approval → exact-action resume → actionable ACS failure propagation passed using an intentionally invalid non-production ACS credential
- Live scheduler: enabled and started, Europe/London, shared-file lease
- Logs: server started, warm-up succeeded, site started, no unhandled startup errors

## Governance settings added

Values were stored in App Service and were not printed or committed.

- Authorized Entra finance approver allowlist
- Approver tenant ID
- Dedicated generated HITL signing secret
- Explicit approver requirement
- Durable single-instance approval, artifact, retrospective, and scheduler lease paths
- Demo approval seeding for the isolated showcase
- Inbound caller default-deny policy and existing CFO caller allowlist
- App Service storage enabled

## Known live limitations

- Azure Monitor/Application Insights is not currently configured in the App Service; stdout and in-memory audit remain active.
- Conversation storage currently reports memory fallback. Mission/HITL showcase state uses durable App Service files, but Cosmos is still required before horizontal scale.
- Agent 365 MCP endpoint is configured, but app-only discovery logs `AADSTS82001`; interactive/OBO tenant permissions still need correction before claiming live WorkIQ parity.
- Cassidy endpoint is configured, while Avatar and AI Kanban specialist endpoints remain unconfigured.
- Direct-route verification proved that an empty browser target uses the configured server default, creates no approval, and reaches ACS immediately. A fresh live click remains required to confirm the tenant call rings after the Teams Phone license remediation.
- This deployment updated the App Service only. It did not publish or modify the Agent 365 blueprint instance or the separate Microsoft Foundry hosted container.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Viewer[YouTube / customer viewer] --> Public[Static preview + minimal health]
  Operator[Signed-in finance operator] --> App[Azure App Service\nMission Control + Trust Center]
  App --> Policy[Server policy + signed HITL]
  App --> Files[Durable single-instance files]
  App --> AOAI[Azure OpenAI]
  App -. configured, tenant permission pending .-> MCP[Agent 365 MCP]
  App -. not configured .-> Monitor[Azure Monitor]
```

